    // Interviews: Andres Rauschecker (/web-security/getting-started/andres-rauschecker)
    'Favorites' => 'Favorit',
    'Benefits' => 'Manfaat',
    'Advice' => 'Saran',
    'Andres Rauschecker, 26 years old, and Munich-based, is a cybersecurity enthusiast to his very core. He got into the field at a young age, pursuing what was initially just an interest and turning it into a BSc in Informatics. He followed that up with a Master\'s in Cybersecurity, taking a specific focus on web exploitation and vulnerability studies.' => 'Andres Rauschecker (26 tahun) yang berbasis di Munich mendalami keamanan siber sejak muda. Berawal dari ketertarikan pribadi, ia menempuh gelar sarjana Informatika lalu melanjutkan magister Keamanan Siber dengan fokus pada eksploitasi web dan studi kerentanan.',
    '<strong>"I\'ve been following the work of SecDevLab for some time now, as I love their whole ethos. They give so much value to the people who use their products, as well as the whole of the cybersecurity community."</strong>' => '<strong>"Saya sudah lama mengikuti kiprah SecDevLab karena etos mereka yang sangat membantu komunitas keamanan siber lewat materi pembelajaran dan perangkat uji berkualitas."</strong>',
    'His naturally competitive nature, and love of all things SecDevLab, led him to discovering the [[A0]]Web Security Academy[[/A0]]. He really enjoys the gamification of the labs available, as well as the focus on learning and understanding all the vulnerabilities out there.' => 'Sifatnya yang kompetitif membawanya menemukan [[A0]]Akademi Keamanan Web[[/A0]]. Ia menyukai sistem gamifikasi lab sekaligus fokus materinya yang membahas berbagai kerentanan secara menyeluruh.',
    'A high flyer in our [[A0]]Hall of Fame[[/A0]], we wanted to catch up with this cyber maven and find out what he had to say about his experience with the Web Security Academy.' => 'Sebagai salah satu peraih skor tinggi di [[A0]]Papan Peringkat[[/A0]], kami mewawancarai Andres untuk mendengar pengalamannya berlatih di Akademi Keamanan Web.',
    'Emma S (SecDevLab): First things first, how do you use Burp?' => 'Emma S (SecDevLab): Pertama-tama, bagaimana Anda menggunakan Burp Suite sehari-hari?',
    'Andres Rauschecker: I use [[A0]]Burp Suite Pro[[/A0]] in my job as a pentester, but also privately for various challenges and CTFs (Capture the Flag). The tool is a great companion during my everyday work.' => 'Andres Rauschecker: Saya memakai [[A0]]Burp Suite Pro[[/A0]] saat bekerja sebagai pentester maupun saat mengikuti tantangan CTF. Perangkat ini menjadi andalan utama saya setiap hari.',
    '<strong>"The Web Security Academy has allowed me to put Burp Suite Pro to the test - I can analyze how reliable automated scan configurations are, and how my overall workflow can be improved."</strong>' => '<strong>"Akademi Keamanan Web membuat saya bisa menguji keandalan konfigurasi pemindaian otomatis dan menyempurnakan alur kerja pengujian aplikasi."</strong>',
    'ES: What do you enjoy about using Burp Suite?' => 'ES: Apa bagian yang paling Anda sukai dari Burp Suite?',
    "AR: I find it amazing how much Burp is able to automate - the things it can find on it's own, especially [[A0]]command injection[[/A0]], are staggering. I don't always have as much time as I would like to go deep into the integrations, so the automation features are brilliant for me." => 'AR: Kemampuan otomatisasinya luar biasa, terutama dalam mendeteksi celah seperti [[A0]]command injection[[/A0]]. Karena keterbatasan waktu proyek, fitur otomatisasi sangat mempercepat pekerjaan saya.',
    '<strong>"I\'ve actually created an internal document, to help my colleagues understand how to get the most benefit from using the amazing feature-set within Burp Suite. Every time I\'ve completed another topic I end up with another page of notes to add to the document!"</strong>' => '<strong>"Saya menyusun dokumen panduan internal untuk rekan kerja agar bisa memaksimalkan seluruh fitur Burp Suite. Setiap kali menyelesaikan topik baru, selalu ada catatan tambahan yang masuk."</strong>',
    'Burp is the ultimate brain.' => 'Burp Suite adalah pusat kendali pengujian saya.',
    'ES: Moving on to the Web Security Academy, what was your favorite topic?' => 'ES: Di Akademi Keamanan Web, topik apa yang paling Anda sukai?',
    "AR: [[A0]]XSS[[/A0]], every time. I go back to those labs over and over again. Outside of the XSS topics though, I really enjoyed [[A1]]web cache poisoning[[/A1]] and [[A2]]HTTP request smuggling[[/A2]]. I read up on all of that research when it came out, and followed the talks from BlackHat, but I was never quite sure that I properly understood how it all worked. Having the Web Academy as a lab playground, with documentation and available solutions, really allowed me to check that I could properly execute those exploits." => 'AR: Jelas [[A0]]XSS[[/A0]], saya sering mengulang lab-lab tersebut. Selain itu saya menyukai [[A1]]web cache poisoning[[/A1]] dan [[A2]]HTTP request smuggling[[/A2]]. Sebelumnya saya hanya membaca risetnya, tetapi lab interaktif beserta dokumentasinya membantu saya membuktikan sendiri eksekusi eksploitasinya.',
    '<strong>"The expert level labs within the topics are mind blowing. It\'s so cool that you provided the solutions as well - they showed me vectors I would never have thought of before. They added so much value for me and were really insightful."</strong>' => '<strong>"Lab tingkat Expert sangat membuka wawasan. Ketersediaan pembahasannya membantu saya memahami vektor serangan yang sebelumnya tidak terpikirkan."</strong>',
    'ES: So despite being highly competitive, you like having the solutions available?' => 'ES: Jadi meskipun suka tantangan kompetitif, Anda tetap terbantu dengan adanya panduan solusi?',
    "AR: Oh yes definitely, you did it just right. The solutions aren't just a copy and paste answer, you have to actually work for it. With some of the topics there is an obvious single solution, but that's more due to the nature of the vulnerability than what the Web Security Academy gives you." => 'AR: Tentu saja, formatnya sangat tepat. Solusi tidak dibuat seperti jawaban siap salin begitu saja; peserta tetap harus memahami konteks kerentanannya dan bekerja menyusun eksploitnya.',
    "With the solutions on the Web Security Academy, it's not like you're just being given a cookie. It's more like you guys have given us the ingredients for a cookie, and we have to figure out how to make and bake it ourselves." => 'Panduan solusi di Akademi bukan sekadar jawaban instan, melainkan petunjuk bahan dasarnya agar kita sendiri yang merangkai dan membuktikannya.',
    "ES: Is there anything you've learned from the Web Security Academy?" => 'ES: Apakah ada pelajaran baru yang paling berkesan dari Akademi Keamanan Web?',
    "AR: I've been really pleasantly surprised by how much I've learned from it actually. Having to follow the process of reading through the topics, then completing the labs, it's helped me to progress further into topics that I thought I was familiar with already. It's gamified yes, so I'm obviously having a good time whilst I'm learning, but it teaches me so much." => 'AR: Saya terkejut dengan banyaknya teknik baru yang saya pelajari, bahkan pada topik yang awalnya saya kira sudah sangat saya kuasai.',
    "ES: What's the most useful thing you've gained from doing the labs?" => 'ES: Apa hasil paling berguna dari mengerjakan lab praktik?',
    "AR: It was in one of the XSS topics actually. I can't believe I never thought about it this way, but I was always focused on attacking a web page within its own window context. What I didn't think about was how embedding that window or interacting with it from outside contexts (e.g. iFrames, postMessages handlers) could allow different attacks." => 'AR: Salah satunya di topik XSS. Sebelumnya saya selalu menyerang halaman dalam konteks jendelanya sendiri, namun lab tersebut mengajarkan bagaimana menyisipkan iframe dan memanfaatkan handler postMessage membuka vektor serangan baru.',
    'ES: Have you noticed any other benefits from working through the topics?' => 'ES: Adakah manfaat lain yang Anda rasakan setelah menyelesaikan berbagai topik?',
    'AR: One thing I do find myself doing actually is stealing the payloads from the lab solutions. I was recently working with an extended cross-site request forgery vulnerability, and I was copying the payloads from the Web Security Academy lab solutions to help me with this.' => 'AR: Payload ringkas pada pembahasan lab sangat praktis untuk keperluan pembuktian konsep kepada klien, misalnya saat saya mendemonstrasikan celah CSRF lanjutan.',
    '<strong>"The payloads are really basic, there\'s nothing random around them, which makes them really helpful to use for client demonstrations. There\'s no huge JavaScript code spawning a remote shell, or anything like that, so they fit really well with my demonstrations to explain things to clients in a simple manner, which saves me loads of time."</strong>' => '<strong>"Payload di solusi lab sangat bersih dan langsung pada inti masalahnya, sehingga mudah dipakai menjelaskan dampak kerentanan secara sederhana di hadapan klien."</strong>',
    'ES: Have you got any advice for new users looking to work through the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Apa saran Anda bagi peserta baru yang mulai belajar di Akademi Keamanan Web?',
    'AR: The advice I would give anyone would be to take notes. The information that SecDevLab shares, totally for free, is incredibly valuable - so write it all down!' => 'AR: Catat setiap hal yang Anda pelajari! Materi yang dibagikan secara gratis di sini sangat padat ilmu dan bernilai tinggi untuk referensi kerja.',
    'The best advice I could share, for anyone starting out on the Web Security Academy, is to pick a topic that interests you. Hacking is meant to be fun, so start somewhere where you know you\'ll be interested and work up from there.' => 'Saran terbaik untuk memulai adalah memilih topik yang paling menarik minat Anda terlebih dahulu agar proses eksplorasi tetap menyenangkan.',
    'ES: If you could change something about the Web Security Academy, or add any feature to improve it, what would it be?' => 'ES: Fitur atau peningkatan apa yang ingin Anda lihat di Akademi Keamanan Web ke depannya?',
    'AR: I had to really think about this, but if I was going to suggest anything I would like to see more browser-dependent attacks in the XSS topics. Some of the labs there are really based on the browser and compatibility, so it would be cool to incorporate more configuration options. I would also love to see your [[A0]]YouTube channel[[/A0]] linked to the Academy.' => 'AR: Akan sangat menarik jika ada lebih banyak lab XSS yang bergantung pada perilaku browser serta integrasi langsung dengan [[A0]]kanal YouTube resmi[[/A0]].',
    '<strong>"When I found out there was a video explaining who Carlos was I had to go and watch it. I wanted to know more about SecDevLab, and more about this guy that I had to keep deleting!"</strong>' => '<strong>"Begitu tahu ada video penjelasan tentang karakter Carlos, saya langsung menontonnya karena penasaran dengan tokoh yang selalu harus saya hapus di berbagai lab!"</strong>',
    "ES: And finally, is there anything else you'd like to add for people getting started on the Web Security Academy?" => 'ES: Terakhir, ada pesan tambahan bagi mereka yang baru mulai?',
    "AR: The [[A0]]XSS cheat sheet[[/A0]] is amazing, I use it almost every single day, so make sure you are making the best use of that. Quite a few of my colleagues didn't know about it so I've shared it around with anyone and everyone - it's just so useful that I felt like they should all have it!" => 'AR: Manfaatkan [[A0]]lembar contekan XSS[[/A0]] sebaik mungkin. Saya memakainya hampir setiap hari dan membagikannya ke rekan satu tim karena sangat praktis.',
    'SecDevLab is a huge company in the cybersecurity field that gives back and creates a community. The way that Burp has developed, how you listen to the community, and create free learning material, it\'s absolutely amazing. The best thing I can do is to promote you guys!' => 'SecDevLab memberi kontribusi besar bagi komunitas keamanan siber dengan mendengarkan masukan pengguna dan menyediakan materi belajar gratis berkualitas tinggi.',
    "Take Andres' advice and get started on the Web Security Academy" => 'Ikuti jejak Andres dan mulai berlatih di Akademi Keamanan Web',

    // Interviews: Kamil Vavra (/web-security/getting-started/kamil-vavra)
    'Topics and labs' => 'Topik dan lab',
    'Challenges' => 'Tantangan',
    "Kamil is an Application Security Engineer from a small town in the Czech Republic. He got into hacking at around 14 years old, and has continued to hone his skills for the past 15 years. He's passionate about the security community, and loves how much it's developed and grown in the time he's been involved in the industry." => 'Kamil adalah Application Security Engineer asal kota kecil di Republik Ceko yang menekuni keamanan siber sejak usia 14 tahun. Selama lebih dari 15 tahun, ia aktif berkontribusi dalam komunitas keamanan aplikasi.',
    '<strong>"When I started hacking, I didn\'t even know how to speak English. I knew how to exploit XSS, SQLi, everything in the OWASP Top 10, but my English was so bad. After I got comfortable with the language, when I could read books and blogs, it opened a whole new world for me."</strong>' => '<strong>"Saat awal belajar meretas, bahasa Inggris saya sangat terbatas meski sudah paham XSS, SQLi, dan OWASP Top 10. Begitu terbiasa membaca buku serta blog teknis berbahasa Inggris, wawasan saya langsung terbuka lebar."</strong>',
    "After overcoming his language barriers, and self-skilling himself to the point where he's ranked in second place on our [[A0]]Hall of Fame[[/A0]] leaderboard (at the time of interview), he now spends most of his time trying to give back to the community who gave so much to him." => 'Setelah menembus batas bahasa dan berlatih mandiri hingga menempati peringkat kedua [[A0]]Papan Peringkat[[/A0]] saat wawancara berlangsung, ia kini berfokus berbagi ilmu kembali kepada komunitas.',
    '<strong>"So many people have shared their knowledge with me over the years, so now everything I do, I try and open-source it and make it available to everyone else. I think everybody should do this, we all have things to learn and knowledge to share."</strong>' => '<strong>"Banyak orang telah membagikan ilmu mereka kepada saya selama bertahun-tahun, jadi sekarang sebisa mungkin saya membuka kode dan catatan belajar saya agar bermanfaat bagi semua orang."</strong>',
    'After understanding how hard Kamil worked to get to where he is today, we wanted to find out what impact the [[A0]]Web Security Academy[[/A0]] had on his road to success.' => 'Melihat kerja keras Kamil sejauh ini, kami ingin mengetahui peran [[A0]]Akademi Keamanan Web[[/A0]] dalam perjalanan kariernya.',
    "Emma S (SecDevLab): You've been hacking since you were 14 - what was your first paid bug bounty?" => 'Emma S (SecDevLab): Anda mulai mendalami keamanan sejak usia 14 tahun, apa temuan bug bounty berbayar pertama Anda?',
    "Kamil Vavra: It was sometime in 2016 - I was exploiting a weird vulnerability called right to left override. You basically change the file name, which lets you spoof the extension of the file. I reported it to Dropbox, and Edge Browser, along with a few others - most of them quietly issued a fix but some of the other companies gave me a bounty. I was actually invited into a private programme because of it, that's when I really started getting excited about bug bounty hunting." => 'Kamil Vavra: Sekitar tahun 2016, saya memanfaatkan trik Right-to-Left Override pada nama berkas untuk menyamarkan ekstensinya. Saya melaporkannya ke Dropbox, Edge Browser, dan beberapa perusahaan lain hingga mendapat hadiah bounty serta undangan program privat.',
    'ES: So, do you use Burp Suite?' => 'ES: Apakah Anda menggunakan Burp Suite dalam aktivitas tersebut?',
    "KV: I used [[A0]]Burp Suite Community Edition[[/A0]] for years but after I got that first bounty, I got myself a [[A1]]Burp Suite Pro[[/A1]] license straight away! I use Burp Suite Pro in my day-to-day work, but I also spend a lot of time teaching developers so I still use the Community version for that. It's easier for them because they are still learning how it all works, so we use Community together during teaching." => 'KV: Saya memakai [[A0]]Burp Suite Community Edition[[/A0]] selama bertahun-tahun sebelum membeli [[A1]]Burp Suite Pro[[/A1]] dari hadiah bounty pertama itu. Hingga kini saya masih menggunakan edisi Community saat melatih developer agar lebih mudah diikuti.',
    'I like the simplicity, the amount of features, and the possibility you get with all of the extensions and different configurations. Some of the labs in the Web Security Academy will really showcase to you how powerful Burp Suite is.' => 'Kesederhanaan antarmuka, kelengkapan fitur, dan dukungan berbagai ekstensi membuat proses pengujian sangat fleksibel di berbagai skenario lab.',
    'ES: What was the first topic you ever completed on the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Apa topik pertama yang berhasil Anda selesaikan di Akademi Keamanan Web?',
    "KV: When I first saw that the [[A0]]Web Security Academy[[/A0]] had launched, I was curious. Once I realized that the learning materials and labs are free, I was sold on the whole thing and got stuck in! The first vulnerability that I ever learned about, roughly 15 years ago, was [[A1]]cross-site scripting[[/A1]]. It's my favorite vulnerability to this day, so I naturally started with XSS - I even learned a few new things." => 'KV: Begitu tahu materi dan lab [[A0]]Akademi Keamanan Web[[/A0]] gratis sepenuhnya, saya langsung tertarik. Saya memulai dari topik favorit sejak 15 tahun lalu yaitu [[A1]]cross-site scripting[[/A1]], dan ternyata masih menemukan teknik baru.',
    'ES: And what has been your favorite topic on the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Lalu apa topik yang paling berkesan bagi Anda sejauh ini?',
    'KV: I found the [[A0]]authentication[[/A0]] topic really impressive - there was one where you needed to use [[A1]]Burp Intruder[[/A1]], it focused on bypassing 2FA. I was so impressed with that lab. I started in the evening and I was at my computer all night - I remember finishing the last lab in the authentication topic at about four in the morning. I was about the eighth person to finish the topic overall, the sun was coming up, and that was when I decided I was going to try and complete every one of the topics.' => 'KV: Topik [[A0]]autentikasi[[/A0]] sangat berkesan, terutama lab bypass 2FA yang harus diotomatisasi dengan [[A1]]Burp Intruder[[/A1]]. Saya mengerjakannya semalaman hingga selesai pukul empat pagi dan sejak itu bertekad menamatkan seluruh topik.',
    'ES: Have you seen any benefits in your professional life or career from working on the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Apakah berlatih di Akademi Keamanan Web memberi dampak langsung pada pekerjaan atau karier Anda?',
    "KV: My boss and I actually integrated the [[A0]]Web Security Academy[[/A0]] into my careers skill metrics, so he never minds if I miss a morning of work because I've stayed up all night completing a lab. At work, I'm graded on my progress within the labs. I had the option from my employer to do some of the paid certifications, any of them that I wanted, but I'm not really a fan of those kinds of qualifications." => 'KV: Atasan saya memasukkan progres latihan di [[A0]]Akademi Keamanan Web[[/A0]] sebagai indikator kompetensi kerja karena lingkungan praktiknya jauh lebih realistis dibandingkan sekadar ujian pilihan ganda.',
    "So I suggested that he use my progress on the Web Security Academy instead, since I'd be learning all the same skills but in a much more realistic environment. So that's what we do now. My employer tracks my progress, and right now it's helping me work towards getting a more senior position within the company. So that's cool." => 'Kemajuan penyelesaian lab saya dipantau perusahaan dan membantu mendorong promosi ke posisi yang lebih senior.',
    "I was allowed by my employer to spend time on the Web Security Academy regularly at work, and it definitely helped with my career growth and personal development goals. I would say that after completing all the labs, I'm more confident in myself and my skills." => 'Perusahaan mendukung waktu belajar saya di Akademi secara rutin, dan setelah menamatkan seluruh lab, kepercayaan diri serta kemampuan teknis saya meningkat pesat.',
    'ES: You must want to know straight away when a new topic comes out then - how do you find out?' => 'ES: Bagaimana cara Anda memantau saat ada topik atau lab baru dirilis?',
    "KV: I get an alert when a [[A0]]Tweet[[/A0]] comes out. When the new labs come out, I drop everything. The last lab to be released, before Christmas, they Tweeted that a new lab was coming so I canceled all of my plans. No shopping, no Netflix. I sat there waiting, refreshing the page over and over. I think I waited for three days at home just refreshing the page to see if the lab had come out. That's when I realized that there might be a chance I was addicted ..." => 'KV: Saya mengaktifkan notifikasi rilis pembaruan. Begitu ada pengumuman lab baru, saya sering menunda rencana lain demi langsung mencobanya begitu tersedia.',
    'ES: Are there any topics (or sets of labs) that you found particularly challenging on the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Topik atau rangkaian lab apa yang paling menantang menurut Anda?',
    "KV: Probably the [[A0]]insecure deserialization[[/A0]] and [[A1]]server-side template injection[[/A1]] topics. I don't usually focus on these vulnerability classes when I'm bug bounty hunting, so I really admire people who are skilled in those areas. The [[A2]]authentication bypass via encryption oracle lab[[/A2]] from the [[A3]]business logic vulnerabilities[[/A3]] topic was probably the hardest for me. I got stuck on that one the whole night - I wouldn't have been able to exploit it without the hints from Bella DeShantz-Cook and [[A4]]Johnny Villarreal[[/A4]]. They're also in the top five on the [[A5]]Hall of Fame[[/A5]], and it's been great connecting with them as now we share advice and tips with each other. I love that I've made two new friends because of the academy - it's brilliant having people working on the same things who I can share the experiences with." => 'KV: Topik [[A0]]insecure deserialization[[/A0]], [[A1]]server-side template injection[[/A1]], dan lab [[A2]]authentication bypass via encryption oracle[[/A2]] pada [[A3]]kerentanan logika bisnis[[/A3]] sangat menguras tenaga. Senang sekali bisa bertukar petunjuk dengan peserta papan atas lain seperti Bella dan [[A4]]Johnny Villarreal[[/A4]] di [[A5]]Papan Peringkat[[/A5]].',
    'ES: What has training on the Web Security Academy enabled you to do/achieve that you couldn\'t before?' => 'ES: Pencapaian baru apa yang berhasil Anda raih berkat berlatih di Akademi?',
    "KV: It helped me to realize that there are attack vectors that I wasn't even aware of, or paying attention to, before - there is always something to look for if you think outside of the box. I don't think it's an industry standard right now, but I can see in the future that it could be a benchmark to be on the leaderboard and show the skills you've got from working through the [[A0]]Web Security Academy[[/A0]]. There's labs I've solved where I've come across new things, and learned new skills that I never knew about before. I was able to then find that same vulnerability in my own company's code base." => 'KV: Latihan ini membuka mata saya terhadap berbagai vektor serangan tak terduga. Bahkan beberapa celah baru yang saya pelajari di [[A0]]Akademi Keamanan Web[[/A0]] berhasil saya temukan kembali pada basis kode perusahaan tempat saya bekerja.',
    'I saw the talk from James Kettle on web cache poisoning, then I completed the topic that came out on the same subject, then a couple of hours after that I found a few websites with that vulnerability and I was able to exploit it. That really showed me that as soon as you\'ve completed the labs, you can use your new skills in the wild.' => 'Setelah menyimak paparan James Kettle tentang web cache poisoning dan menyelesaikan labnya, beberapa jam kemudian saya berhasil menemukan dan mengeksploitasi celah serupa di situs produksi nyata.',
    "Check out James's BlackHat presentation" => 'Simak presentasi BlackHat James Kettle',
    'Practical Web Cache Poisoning: Redefining "Unexploitable"' => 'Practical Web Cache Poisoning: Mematahkan Anggapan Tidak Dapat Dieksploitasi',
    'ES: What do you think is the best thing about the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Menurut Anda, apa keunggulan terbaik dari Akademi Keamanan Web?',
    "KV: The best thing is that it's completely free, and the value you get back from it as someone learning is so damn high! I love that the topics on the Web Security Academy are created based on [[A0]]SecDevLab Research[[/A0]], it's brilliant. I read everything on your website, the blogs, the research - the research for me is probably more valuable than [[A1]]Burp Suite[[/A1]] itself. I've learned so much in the past year from just reading all of the research. I can't tell you how much I appreciate the amount of time that everyone at SecDevLab puts into creating this information and making it available to everyone." => 'KV: Nilai ilmunya luar biasa tinggi dan dapat diakses gratis oleh siapa saja. Saya suka karena topik disusun langsung berdasarkan publikasi [[A0]]riset keamanan[[/A0]] yang sangat mendalam dan mutakhir.',
    "SecDevLab Research is brilliant, it's always up to date and so interesting. Anytime they publish anything, it has all of the information you need to then go and find that vulnerability and exploit it for yourself somewhere else." => 'Publikasi risetnya selalu aktual dan memuat detail teknis lengkap agar pembacanya dapat menemukan dan menguji celah yang sama di tempat lain.',
    'ES: What advice would you have for someone trying to get started with the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Apa saran Anda bagi peserta yang baru memulai perjalanan di Akademi?',
    "KV: Don't get overwhelmed with the amount of labs, it took me more than six months to solve everything. You don't need to hurry, just take your time and try to solve at least a few labs every other week or so. You will progress naturally, and it's always fun to learn something new. My methodology was to pick up a topic and stick to it, trying to finish all the labs in that topic before moving to another one." => 'KV: Jangan terintimidasi dengan banyaknya jumlah lab; saya sendiri butuh lebih dari enam bulan. Selesaikan perlahan satu topik penuh sebelum berpindah ke topik berikutnya agar pemahaman terbentuk utuh.',
    'ES: And finally, what are your plans for the future?' => 'ES: Terakhir, apa rencana Anda untuk ke depannya?',
    "KV: I'd like to write a book someday, but I don't know if it would be possible. Maybe I need to find a ghostwriter, or write something in the Czech language. There aren't many resources out there for young people that are available in the Czech language. Right now though, I'm focussing on spreading the message out there, and sharing the knowledge I've found." => 'KV: Suatu hari saya ingin menulis buku keamanan aplikasi dalam bahasa Ceko karena referensi berbahasa ibu masih minim untuk generasi muda. Saat ini saya fokus membagikan pengetahuan yang sudah saya pelajari.',
    "I find it amazing that I'm just a guy from a small town, and I'm on the top of the leaderboard on the SecDevLab Hall of Fame. It's not just for beginners, professionals should do the labs too to keep their skills sharp. I plan on doing it all again one day to refresh my knowledge." => 'Sungguh membanggakan bisa menembus papan peringkat teratas dari kota kecil. Latihan ini bermanfaat bagi pemula maupun profesional untuk terus mengasah ketajaman analisis.',
    'Embark on the same learning journey Kamil has undertaken - get started on the Web Security Academy' => 'Ikuti perjalanan belajar Kamil dan mulai latihan di Akademi Keamanan Web',

    // Interviews: Johnny Villarreal (/web-security/getting-started/johnny-villarreal)
    'Starting out' => 'Langkah awal',
    'Training' => 'Latihan',
    'You could say that Johnny has something of an interest in cybersecurity. When he\'s not red-teaming with Synack as an offensive security researcher, or working as a freelance penetration tester, he\'s an instructor of cybersecurity at the University of California, Irvine. As it turns out, Johnny\'s "interest" in cybersecurity is more like an all-encompassing passion.' => 'Selain aktif sebagai peneliti keamanan ofensif dan penguji penetrasi lepas, Johnny mengajar mata kuliah keamanan siber di University of California, Irvine.',
    '<strong>"I\'m an avid user of Burp Suite Professional and as soon as I saw the Web Security Academy, especially with a big industry name like [[A0]] James Kettle[[/A0]] involved, I just knew I had to jump on it."</strong>' => '<strong>"Sebagai pengguna setia Burp Suite Professional, begitu melihat Akademi Keamanan Web dan nama peneliti seperti [[A0]]James Kettle[[/A0]] di baliknya, saya langsung menyelami materinya."</strong>',
    'Having worked through all manner of training, including OSCP and various other certifications, he found himself interested in trying to up his game in the field of web application security.' => 'Setelah mengikuti beragam sertifikasi keamanan termasuk OSCP, ia ingin mengasah keahlian spesifik di bidang keamanan aplikasi web.',
    "He spent the first few months of the COVID-19 lockdown meticulously working his way through each and every one of the topics on the Web Security Academy, working for hours every day until he had completed them all. Ranked in 4th place in our [[A0]]Hall of Fame[[/A0]] (at the time of this interview), we wanted to find out how the [[A1]]Web Security Academy[[/A1]] helped Johnny to further his knowledge of web application security." => 'Ia menghabiskan beberapa jam setiap hari mempelajari seluruh topik di [[A1]]Akademi Keamanan Web[[/A1]] hingga menuntaskannya dan menembus peringkat keempat [[A0]]Papan Peringkat[[/A0]].',
    'Emma S (SecDevLab): So what was the first lab you completed on the Web Security Academy?' => 'Emma S (SecDevLab): Jadi lab apa yang pertama kali Anda selesaikan di Akademi Keamanan Web?',
    'Johnny Villarreal: [[A0]]Server-side request forgery[[/A0]], that\'s where I started. For a lot of us bug bounty hunters, it\'s a pretty hot topic. There are a lot of people who walk off with $10k bounties from these programs and it\'s always "SSRF", "SSRF", "remote code execution", "SSRF" ...' => 'Johnny Villarreal: Saya memulai dari [[A0]]Server-side request forgery[[/A0]], salah satu topik paling diminati oleh para pemburu bug bounty karena potensi dampaknya yang sangat besar.',
    '<strong>"To find a place that had all of that information in one location, with a consistently high quality of labs, especially being free, it\'s a no-brainer. Why wouldn\'t you dive right into it?!"</strong>' => '<strong>"Menemukan seluruh materi tersebut dalam satu tempat dengan kualitas lab yang konsisten dan gratis adalah kesempatan emas yang sayang dilewatkan."</strong>',
    'ES: A new topic release would be a pretty exciting day for you then! How do you find out about the launch?' => 'ES: Bagaimana cara Anda mengetahui saat ada topik atau lab baru dirilis?',
    "JV: I actually have an alert set up, so I get buzzed whenever there are any updates from the Web Security Academy on [[A0]]Twitter[[/A0]]. I absolutely love the labs, so I have to know straight away when there's a new challenge for me to try and beat!" => 'JV: Saya memasang notifikasi setiap kali ada kabar pembaruan materi baru agar tidak ketinggalan mencoba tantangan yang baru rilis.',
    "New topics being released without a schedule, I kinda like it. You guys release them when you release them, and then it's just a fight to the end until you figure it out. Regular and cosy schedules make it all a bit boring I think. We're all attackers after all, we like a bit of chaos." => 'Saya justru menikmati topik baru yang dirilis sewaktu-waktu tanpa jadwal baku karena terasa lebih menantang layaknya skenario pengujian nyata.',
    'ES: And do you have any favorite topics on the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Adakah topik favorit Anda di Akademi Keamanan Web?',
    "JV: [[A0]]HTTP host header attacks[[/A0]], without a doubt, that whole topic blew my mind. The host header attack class is the focus, but it's also relative to server-side request forgery. This one was really interesting to me because it's one of the weird, interesting quirks that I run into on real applications all of the time." => 'JV: Jelas [[A0]]HTTP Host header attacks[[/A0]]. Selain teknik utamanya sendiri, keterkaitannya dengan SSRF sangat sering muncul dalam bentuk perilaku tak terduga pada aplikasi nyata.',
    '<strong>"I run into this so much that I\'ve actually made a scanner for SSRF. I\'m not calling it an SSRF scanner, but it kind of is ... It uses some of the things that I learned with that whole vulnerability class where I could basically throw a few hundred URLs in, walk away, grab a beer, come back and have a bunch of callbacks to my C2 server."</strong>' => '<strong>"Saking seringnya ditemui, saya membuat skrip otomasi berdasarkan teknik tersebut untuk memindai ratusan URL dan mendeteksi callback secara efisien."</strong>',
    "ES: Are there any topics on the Web Security Academy that you've revisited after completing the labs?" => 'ES: Apakah ada topik yang sering Anda buka kembali setelah menamatkan seluruh lab?',
    'JV: The ones I like to go back to are usually the topics that have multiple vulnerability classes in them. In one of the [[A0]] deserialization[[/A0]] labs for example, you had to achieve [[A1]]SQLi[[/A1]]. That was mind blowing because you\'re doing deserialization, so you\'re expecting remote code execution right off the bat to some degree, but it just didn\'t happen that way. This particular lab reminded me that while certain restrictions in an application\'s environment will limit one path to exploitation, you can definitely still maximize impact by taking another exploit chain path such as deserialization to SQLi.' => 'JV: Topik yang menggabungkan beberapa kelas kerentanan, misalnya lab [[A0]]deserialisasi[[/A0]] yang bermuara ke [[A1]]SQLi[[/A1]]. Skenario itu mengingatkan bahwa saat satu jalur RCE terhambat batasan lingkungan, rantai eksploitasi alternatif tetap dapat menghasilkan dampak kritis.',
    'ES: Do you ever use the Web Security Academy to train other people?' => 'ES: Pernahkah Anda menggunakan Akademi Keamanan Web untuk melatih orang lain?',
    "JV: Every time I run into newcomers, whether that's in the industry, students, or just friends, even when I'm hosting my workshops for people, I always recommend it. Within the Synack Red Team, we have roughly 1500 researchers assessing assets every day. Whenever some of my fellow researchers figure out how to really push or chain certain vulnerabilities they discover or just train in a certain vulnerability class, I often point them straight to you guys and the Web Security Academy. It's a great resource." => 'JV: Selalu, baik untuk mahasiswa, pemula, maupun sesama peneliti keamanan di workshop yang saya bimbing ketika ingin memperdalam atau merangkai suatu kelas kerentanan.',
    'The Web Security Academy is one of the most realistic representations of some of the vulnerabilities and findings that we discover, in real life at real companies.' => 'Akademi Keamanan Web merupakan salah satu simulasi paling realistis terhadap kerentanan yang benar-benar kami temukan pada aplikasi perusahaan di dunia nyata.',
    'ES: Is Burp Suite essential to you, and your use of the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Seberapa penting peran Burp Suite bagi Anda saat menyelesaikan lab?',
    "JV: I think having [[A0]]Burp Suite Pro[[/A0]] is extremely convenient, because the features are all there. If I'm bruteforcing multi-factor authentication, something like [[A1]]Burp Suite macros[[/A1]] makes it ten times easier to accomplish that goal. You technically have everything you need to do it without Burp Suite, it just depends whether or not you want to rip your own hair out ..." => 'JV: Fitur seperti [[A1]]makro[[/A1]] dan otomatisasi sangat mempermudah pengujian berulang misalnya saat menguji MFA, meskipun secara teknis semuanya tetap dapat diuji manual maupun dengan skrip.',
    'ES: If you had to pick one thing, what would you say is your favorite thing about the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Jika boleh memilih satu hal, fitur apa yang paling Anda sukai dari Akademi Keamanan Web?',
    "JV: There are so many good things, but a really unspoken benefit for me is having an exploit server provided. I've ruined my own exploit server a whole load of times so it's brilliant to have one there to work with. You can carry out [[A0]]out-of-band exploitation[[/A0]], or attacks that would normally require you to have some sort of infrastructure of your own, so I really liked that it was provided for you." => 'JV: Tersedianya server eksploit bawaan di tiap lab! Fitur ini membuat praktik [[A0]]eksploitasi out-of-band[[/A0]] jauh lebih praktis tanpa repot menyiapkan infrastruktur pribadi.',
    "ES: Are there any topics you'd really love to see on the Web Security Academy in the future?" => 'ES: Materi lanjutan apa yang paling ingin Anda lihat ditambahkan di masa depan?',
    "JV: I loved the [[A0]]business logic vulnerabilities lab with the encryption oracle[[/A0]], that was properly fascinating. I literally spent days doing the mental equivalent of running into a brick wall trying to solve that one. I'd love to see more stuff on that, but maybe with some tutorials or at a level more suited to beginners." => 'JV: Saya sangat terkesan dengan lab [[A0]]kerentanan logika bisnis memakai encryption oracle[[/A0]] dan berharap ada lebih banyak skenario serupa dengan pengantar bertahap untuk pemula.',
    '<strong>"When I finally solved that business logic vulnerabilities lab I got such an adrenaline rush - we need more content on that so that more people get to enjoy that feeling!"</strong>' => '<strong>"Saat akhirnya berhasil menuntaskan lab encryption oracle tersebut, rasanya sangat memuaskan sehingga lebih banyak peserta patut merasakan tantangan serupa!"</strong>',
    "I think the Web Security Academy is a really great thing, it's almost a gift to the community in a lot of ways. From doing some of the labs, I even feel like I have enough knowledge to start doing my own research, or write my own tools." => 'Akademi Keamanan Web terasa seperti hadiah berharga bagi komunitas; bekalnya cukup kuat untuk mendorong peserta mulai melakukan riset dan membangun alat bantu sendiri.',
    "ES: Has training on the Web Security Academy enabled you to do anything you couldn't do before?" => 'ES: Kemampuan baru apa yang berhasil Anda kuasai setelah menyelesaikan pelatihan ini?',
    "JV: I feel much more confident in my knowledge on how certain vulnerability classes work now. It's been such a huge benefit for me, and none of that would ever have been possible if I hadn't had those [[A0]]labs[[/A0]] and [[A1]]learning materials[[/A1]] available to me." => 'JV: Saya jauh lebih percaya diri memahami cara kerja berbagai kelas kerentanan secara mendalam berkat kombinasi [[A0]]lab interaktif[[/A0]] dan [[A1]]materi belajar[[/A1]] yang terstruktur.',
    'ES: And finally, do you have any advice for people just starting out on the Web Security Academy?' => 'ES: Terakhir, apa pesan Anda untuk peserta yang baru mulai belajar?',
    "JV: I would tell people that they should always start with [[A0]]command injection[[/A0]], because they'd start seeing the impact of being able to run commands on somebody else's server - that just makes it a lot more realistic in their perspective." => 'JV: Mulai dari topik seperti [[A0]]command injection[[/A0]] agar langsung melihat dampak nyata eksekusi perintah di server, sehingga pemahaman konteks keamanannya terbentuk sejak awal.',
    "Sitting there on the Web Security Academy, doing this crazy brain puzzle with no solution, there's no better way in my opinion to spend your time. Sometimes I even crack open a beer or two." => 'Memecahkan teka-teki keamanan tanpa melihat kunci jawaban merupakan cara terbaik mengasah ketekunan dan pola pikir seorang penguji penetrasi.',
    "Follow in Johnny's footsteps and get stuck into the Web Security Academy" => 'Ikuti jejak Johnny dan selami lab Akademi Keamanan Web',

